<% content_for :title, "Overlay & Presence" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Primitives</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Overlay &amp; Presence</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    The two cross-cutting behaviours every overlay in the kit is built from:
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--presence</code>, which holds an element in the page until its exit
    animation has finished, and <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--overlay</code>, which places it in the
    browser&rsquo;s top layer, dismisses it and gives focus back. Everything on this page is driven by those two
    controllers on plain markup — no components involved.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Demo-only glue: the primitives' public API is a value and two events, so the buttons that
    sit outside a presence element flip its value, and the dismissal guard is an ordinary
    listener on the cancelable event -- which is exactly how Modal's unsaved-changes
    confirmation will hook into it. %>
<style>
  /* Classic, space-taking scrollbars on this page, so the scroll lock's "no horizontal shift"
     guarantee is actually exercised here: macOS overlay scrollbars reserve no width at all. */
  html::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 15px; }
  html::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb { background: #a3a3a3; border-radius: 8px; }
</style>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Presence</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4">
  The controlled element carries <code class="font-mono text-xs">data-state="open&nbsp;|&nbsp;closing&nbsp;|&nbsp;closed"</code>
  and nothing else: no classes are added or removed. Closing leaves it visible and laid out at
  <code class="font-mono text-xs">closing</code> until its own animation reports done, then hides it with the
  <code class="font-mono text-xs">hidden</code> attribute. An element with no declared transition closes in the same
  frame, and under <code class="font-mono text-xs">prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code> so does one that has.
</p>

<div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-8 mb-8 space-y-6">
  <div>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
      <button id="fade-open" data-presence="fade-panel" data-presence-open="true"
              class="rounded-md bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-white dark:text-neutral-900">Open</button>
      <button id="fade-close" data-presence="fade-panel" data-presence-open="false"
              class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">Close</button>
      <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">500ms fade + slide</span>
    </div>
    <div id="fade-panel"
         data-controller="ui--presence"
         class="rounded-md border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 p-4 text-sm
                transition duration-500 ease-out
                data-[state=closed]:opacity-0 data-[state=closed]:-translate-y-2
                data-[state=closing]:opacity-0 data-[state=closing]:-translate-y-2"
         hidden>
      I stay in the page, laid out, for the whole 500ms of my exit animation. Only when it finishes does
      <code class="font-mono text-xs">data-state</code> become <code class="font-mono text-xs">closed</code> and the
      <code class="font-mono text-xs">hidden</code> attribute come back.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
      <button id="instant-open" data-presence="instant-panel" data-presence-open="true"
              class="rounded-md bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-white dark:text-neutral-900">Open</button>
      <button id="instant-close" data-presence="instant-panel" data-presence-open="false"
              class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">Close</button>
      <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">no transition declared</span>
    </div>
    <div id="instant-panel"
         data-controller="ui--presence"
         class="rounded-md border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 p-4 text-sm"
         hidden>
      Nothing is declared on me, so I close in the same frame — the primitive measures rather than waits.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Overlay</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4">
  Three modes, each one a platform primitive: <code class="font-mono text-xs">modal</code> is a
  <code class="font-mono text-xs">&lt;dialog&gt;</code> opened with <code class="font-mono text-xs">showModal()</code>,
  <code class="font-mono text-xs">layer</code> is <code class="font-mono text-xs">popover="auto"</code>, and
  <code class="font-mono text-xs">hint</code> is <code class="font-mono text-xs">popover="manual"</code>. Paint order,
  Escape ordering and light dismiss come with them &mdash; that is all placement in the top layer. Where a panel
  actually sits is <%= link_to "ui--anchor", primitives_navigation_path, class: "underline" %>&rsquo;s: the layer and
  hint demos below compose both, anchored to their triggers, the way a real menu or tooltip is. The modals stay
  centred, because a dialog should.
</p>

<div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-8 mb-8">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">

    <%# Modal, with a layer and a second modal nested inside it %>
    <div id="modal-overlay"
         data-controller="ui--overlay"
         data-ui--overlay-mode-value="modal"
         data-ui--overlay-scroll-lock-value="true">
      <button id="modal-trigger"
              data-ui--overlay-target="trigger"
              data-action="click->ui--overlay#toggle"
              class="rounded-md bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-white dark:text-neutral-900">
        Open modal
      </button>

      <dialog id="modal-content"
              data-ui--overlay-target="content"
              aria-labelledby="modal-title"
              class="mx-auto mt-10 mb-auto w-full max-w-lg max-h-[40vh] overflow-y-auto rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700
                     bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 p-6 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50 shadow-xl backdrop:bg-neutral-950/50
                     transition duration-300 ease-out
                     data-[state=open]:scale-100
                     data-[state=closed]:opacity-0 data-[state=closed]:scale-95
                     data-[state=closing]:opacity-0 data-[state=closing]:scale-95">
        <h3 id="modal-title" class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">A modal overlay</h3>
        <p id="modal-text" class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4">
          The focus trap, the top layer and Escape are the browser&rsquo;s. The scroll lock, the backdrop click and
          the exit animation are the primitive&rsquo;s. Drag-select this sentence out onto the backdrop and let go —
          the overlay stays open, because the gesture began inside it.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <%# A layer opened inside a modal: in the top layer too, so it is neither clipped by
              this dialog's scroll box nor painted behind it, and Escape closes it first. %>
          <div id="inner-layer-overlay" data-controller="ui--overlay" data-ui--overlay-mode-value="layer">
            <button id="inner-layer-trigger"
                    data-ui--overlay-target="trigger"
                    data-action="click->ui--overlay#toggle"
                    class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
              Open a layer inside
            </button>
            <div id="inner-layer-content"
                 data-ui--overlay-target="content"
                 role="menu"
                 aria-label="Nested layer"
                 class="m-auto rounded-md border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 p-2 text-sm shadow-xl
                        transition duration-200 ease-out
                        data-[state=closed]:opacity-0 data-[state=closed]:scale-95
                        data-[state=closing]:opacity-0 data-[state=closing]:scale-95">
              <button role="menuitem" class="block w-full rounded px-3 py-1.5 text-left hover:bg-neutral-100 dark:hover:bg-neutral-800">Rename</button>
              <button role="menuitem" class="block w-full rounded px-3 py-1.5 text-left hover:bg-neutral-100 dark:hover:bg-neutral-800">Duplicate</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <%# A second lock-requesting overlay: closing it must not unlock the page under the first. %>
          <div id="nested-overlay"
               data-controller="ui--overlay"
               data-ui--overlay-mode-value="modal"
               data-ui--overlay-scroll-lock-value="true">
            <button id="nested-modal-trigger"
                    data-ui--overlay-target="trigger"
                    data-action="click->ui--overlay#toggle"
                    class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
              Open a second modal
            </button>
            <dialog id="nested-modal-content"
                    data-ui--overlay-target="content"
                    aria-labelledby="nested-modal-title"
                    class="m-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 p-6
                           text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50 shadow-xl backdrop:bg-neutral-950/50
                           transition duration-300 ease-out
                           data-[state=closed]:opacity-0 data-[state=closing]:opacity-0">
              <h3 id="nested-modal-title" class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Second modal</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4">
                Closing me leaves the page locked, because the modal underneath still holds a lock.
              </p>
              <button id="nested-modal-close"
                      data-action="click->ui--overlay#close"
                      class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
                Close
              </button>
            </dialog>
          </div>

          <button id="modal-close"
                  data-action="click->ui--overlay#close"
                  class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
            Close
          </button>
        </div>
      </dialog>
    </div>

    <%# A standalone layer: light dismiss, Escape and paint order are the browser's; position is
        ui--anchor's, wired the same way Popover and Tooltip wire it, just written out here
        instead of behind their controllers. %>
    <div id="menu-overlay" data-controller="ui--overlay ui--anchor"
         data-ui--overlay-mode-value="layer"
         data-ui--anchor-placement-value="bottom-start"
         data-ui--anchor-offset-value="8"
         data-ui--anchor-strategy-value="fixed">
      <button id="menu-trigger"
              data-ui--overlay-target="trigger"
              data-ui--anchor-target="anchor"
              data-action="click->ui--overlay#toggle"
              class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
        Open layer
      </button>
      <div id="menu-content"
           data-ui--overlay-target="content"
           data-ui--anchor-target="floating"
           role="menu"
           aria-label="Standalone layer"
           class="rounded-md border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 p-2 text-sm shadow-xl
                  transition duration-200 ease-out
                  data-[state=closed]:opacity-0 data-[state=closed]:scale-95
                  data-[state=closing]:opacity-0 data-[state=closing]:scale-95">
        <button id="menu-item-edit" role="menuitem" class="block w-full rounded px-3 py-1.5 text-left hover:bg-neutral-100 dark:hover:bg-neutral-800">Edit</button>
        <button role="menuitem" class="block w-full rounded px-3 py-1.5 text-left hover:bg-neutral-100 dark:hover:bg-neutral-800">Delete</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# A hint: manual, so it never light-dismisses the layer the pointer is inside %>
    <div id="hint-overlay" data-controller="ui--overlay ui--anchor"
         data-ui--overlay-mode-value="hint"
         data-ui--anchor-placement-value="top"
         data-ui--anchor-offset-value="6"
         data-ui--anchor-strategy-value="fixed">
      <button id="hint-trigger"
              data-ui--overlay-target="trigger"
              data-ui--anchor-target="anchor"
              data-action="click->ui--overlay#toggle"
              class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
        Show hint
      </button>
      <div id="hint-content"
           data-ui--overlay-target="content"
           data-ui--anchor-target="floating"
           role="tooltip"
           class="rounded-md bg-neutral-900 px-2 py-1 text-xs text-white shadow-lg
                  transition duration-150 data-[state=closed]:opacity-0 data-[state=closing]:opacity-0">
        Escape dismisses me without closing anything underneath.
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# A dismissal a listener vetoes -- the seam Modal's unsaved-changes guard uses %>
    <div id="guarded-overlay"
         data-controller="ui--overlay"
         data-ui--overlay-mode-value="modal"
         data-ui--overlay-scroll-lock-value="true">
      <button id="guarded-trigger"
              data-ui--overlay-target="trigger"
              data-action="click->ui--overlay#toggle"
              class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
        Open guarded modal
      </button>
      <dialog id="guarded-content"
              data-ui--overlay-target="content"
              aria-labelledby="guarded-title"
              class="m-auto w-full max-w-md rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 p-6
                     text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50 shadow-xl backdrop:bg-neutral-950/50
                     transition duration-300 data-[state=closed]:opacity-0 data-[state=closing]:opacity-0">
        <h3 id="guarded-title" class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Guarded modal</h3>
        <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm mb-4">
          <input id="guard-toggle" type="checkbox" checked class="rounded border-neutral-300">
          Refuse Escape and backdrop dismissal
        </label>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4">
          A listener on <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--overlay:dismiss</code> calls
          <code class="font-mono text-xs">preventDefault()</code> while that box is ticked. The Close button below
          closes programmatically, which never asks.
        </p>
        <button id="guarded-close"
                data-action="click->ui--overlay#close"
                class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
          Close
        </button>
      </dialog>
    </div>

    <%# Removed from the page while open: the lock and the focus still come back %>
    <div id="removable-overlay"
         data-controller="ui--overlay"
         data-ui--overlay-mode-value="modal"
         data-ui--overlay-scroll-lock-value="true">
      <button id="removable-trigger"
              data-ui--overlay-target="trigger"
              data-action="click->ui--overlay#toggle"
              class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
        Open removable modal
      </button>
      <dialog id="removable-content"
              data-ui--overlay-target="content"
              aria-labelledby="removable-title"
              class="m-auto w-full max-w-md rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 p-6
                     text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50 shadow-xl backdrop:bg-neutral-950/50
                     transition duration-300 data-[state=closed]:opacity-0 data-[state=closing]:opacity-0">
        <h3 id="removable-title" class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Removable modal</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4">
          A Turbo Stream that empties this overlay&rsquo;s container never runs its close. Removal is a close:
          the page unlocks and focus goes back to the trigger anyway.
        </p>
        <button id="remove-overlay"
                class="rounded-md border border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium">
          Remove me from the DOM
        </button>
      </dialog>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Values</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Controller</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["ui--presence", "open",          "false",    "Boolean. The whole API: true enters, false exits."],
        ["ui--presence", "timeout",       "1000",     "Number, ms. Ceiling on the safety timer derived from the element's computed duration."],
        ["ui--overlay",  "open",          "false",    "Boolean. Ignored until the controller has connected."],
        ["ui--overlay",  "mode",          '"layer"',  "modal (<dialog>), layer (popover=auto) or hint (popover=manual)."],
        ["ui--overlay",  "dismissible",   "true",     "Whether Escape and outside clicks may dismiss it at all."],
        ["ui--overlay",  "scrollLock",    "false",    "Locks body scroll while open, reference-counted across every open overlay."],
        ["ui--overlay",  "restoreFocus",  "true",     "Returns focus to the trigger on close, including after Escape or removal."],
        ["ui--overlay",  "initialFocus",  '""',       "Selector, resolved within the content target, for what takes focus on open."],
        ["ui--overlay",  "moveFocus",     "true",     "Whether opening moves focus into the content at all. false is for a layer that must not steal it, the way a hint never does."]
      ].each do |controller, name, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= controller %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Targets &amp; events</h2>
<ul class="mb-8 space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
  <li><code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--presence</code> — no targets; it operates on its own element. Emits
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--presence:opened</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--presence:closing</code>
    and <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--presence:closed</code>. Actions: <code class="font-mono text-xs">open</code>,
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">close</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs">toggle</code>.</li>
  <li><code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--overlay</code> — targets <code class="font-mono text-xs">content</code> (required),
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">trigger</code> and <code class="font-mono text-xs">backdrop</code>. It writes
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">aria-expanded</code> on the trigger, and <code class="font-mono text-xs">aria-controls</code>
    naming the content unless the trigger already has one (a combobox names its listbox). Emits
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--overlay:opened</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--overlay:closed</code> and
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">ui--overlay:dismiss</code>, the last one cancelable: calling
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">preventDefault()</code> on it keeps the overlay open. It names the gesture in
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">event.detail.reason</code> &mdash; <code class="font-mono text-xs">"escape"</code>,
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">"outside"</code> or <code class="font-mono text-xs">"programmatic"</code> &mdash; so a
    listener can refuse one and allow the rest, the way Modal&rsquo;s
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">close_on_backdrop: false</code> does.</li>
  <li>Style the states, don&rsquo;t hide them: presence owns the <code class="font-mono text-xs">hidden</code> attribute, so
    keep <code class="font-mono text-xs">display</code> out of your <code class="font-mono text-xs">data-state</code> rules
    or the exit animation has nothing to animate.</li>
</ul>

<%# Room to scroll, so the scroll lock has something to hold still. %>
<div class="h-[150vh]" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<script>
  // Buttons that sit outside a presence element drive it through its value, which is the
  // controller's whole public API.
  document.addEventListener("click", function (event) {
    var button = event.target.closest("[data-presence]");
    if (!button) return;
    var panel = document.getElementById(button.dataset.presence);
    panel.setAttribute("data-ui--presence-open-value", button.dataset.presenceOpen);
  });

  // The overlay whose content leaves the page while it is open, the way a Turbo Stream that
  // empties its container does. No close() runs; the primitive treats the removal as one.
  document.addEventListener("click", function (event) {
    if (!event.target.closest("#remove-overlay")) return;
    document.getElementById("removable-content").remove();
  });

  // ui--anchor only computes and tracks position while active, so it has to be told when the
  // layer and hint panels it positions are actually open -- the same wiring ui--popover and
  // ui--tooltip do for Popover and Tooltip, written out here instead of behind their controllers.
  ["menu-overlay", "hint-overlay"].forEach(function (id) {
    var overlay = document.getElementById(id);
    overlay.addEventListener("ui--overlay:opened", function () {
      overlay.setAttribute("data-ui--anchor-active-value", "true");
    });
    overlay.addEventListener("ui--overlay:closed", function () {
      overlay.setAttribute("data-ui--anchor-active-value", "false");
    });
  });

  // The vetoable dismissal, as an ordinary listener on the cancelable event.
  document.addEventListener("ui--overlay:dismiss", function (event) {
    if (event.target.id !== "guarded-overlay") return;
    if (document.getElementById("guard-toggle").checked) event.preventDefault();
  });
</script>
